AIM

To demonstrate various data types and operators in Python using a simple Python program.

ALGORITHM
Start the program.
Declare variables using different data types such as integer, float, string, Boolean, list, tuple, set, and dictionary.
Display the data type of each variable.
Declare two numeric variables.
Perform arithmetic operations such as addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, modulus, and exponentiation.
Perform comparison operations.
Perform logical operations using Boolean values.
Demonstrate assignment, membership, and identity operators.
Display the results.
Stop the program.

SOURCE CODE

# Demonstration of Data Types and Operators in Python

# Data Types
a = 10
b = 5.5
name = "Suyash"
student = True
numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4]
coordinates = (10, 20)
fruits = {"Apple", "Banana", "Mango"}
details = {"Name": "Suyash", "Age": 20}

print("DATA TYPES")
print(a, type(a))
print(b, type(b))
print(name, type(name))
print(student, type(student))
print(numbers, type(numbers))
print(coordinates, type(coordinates))
print(fruits, type(fruits))
